      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The stability argument is a weak attempt to deflect from the fact that the electoral college inherently favors the interests of rural, white, and affluent voters over the interests of urban, minority, and low-income voters. Addressing this argument in your paper will only serve to further legitimize the status quo, but if you want to provide a nuanced critique, you could say: \"While some argue that the electoral college provides stability by forcing candidates to build broad coalitions, this claim ignores the fact that the system's inherent biases and disproportionate representation of rural areas create a self-perpetuating cycle of inequality, ultimately undermining the very stability it purports to maintain.\"",
      "source": "target",
